I made no game changes this run, so no screen has a new critic score and none has reached 4.

- **Camera blocked:** the `run` tool refused `tools/uishots.ps1` both times I tried it (with and without `-NoLint`, port 9353). I couldn't take fresh before or after pictures.
- **No current pictures:** the newest pictures on disk are older than the last ships. They predate the v31.59–v31.61 settings changes for some screens. For the raid pause box (25) they predate the pset6 and pset8 pause-box fixes. Grading them would judge old builds, so I didn't re-grade them.
- **Critic check:** the critic does run. It scored the old raid pause box (25) a 3. Its findings were the 72px report row, the loud abandon button and the stray lime tab. Ships pset6 and pset8 already addressed all three.
- **No blind changes:** I didn't ship UI changes I couldn't see or have graded.

I wrote what the next run needs into `tools/handoff/console/notes/c-31-ui-pause-settings.md`. It needs the camera working. Then it should shoot 18, 25, 26, 32, 42, 49, 70, 72, 74 and 75, grade them with the critic, and carry on with the open items:
- snap the settings list to whole rows;
- section labels before the keys and pad rows;
- lb/rb glyphs at the tab ends;
- pad focus staging for 74 and 75;
- the 42 and 49 pause boxes, which are still untouched.

TASK PARTIAL: the camera was refused this run, so no new pictures or critic scores. Next run: shoot first, then the open items above.
